<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/dir-languages>
    a stt:Document ;
    dcterms:identifier "dir-languages" ;
    dcterms:title "Stakeholder directive: Kotlin library first, Rust library second" ;
    rdfs:comment """Given by the requester on 2026-10-20 when commissioning these requirements: "API requirements are intended for kotlin (first) and rust (second) libraries."""" .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/dir-targets>
    a stt:Document ;
    dcterms:identifier "dir-targets" ;
    dcterms:title "Stakeholder directive: transpile targets and API-first" ;
    rdfs:comment "Given by the requester on 2026-10-20: Kotlin targets Node, Java (JVM) and Android; Rust targets WebAssembly. The API set is to be defined and reviewed first, in an OpenAPI-like but non-REST definition." .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/dir-journeys>
    a stt:Document ;
    dcterms:identifier "dir-journeys" ;
    dcterms:title "Stakeholder directive: the library must carry the workshop user journeys" ;
    rdfs:comment """Given by the requester on 2026-10-20 (DRAFT journeys J1 to J5, a cross-border birth and routine vaccination storyline): J1 a clinic in Country A issues a DVC for newborn routine vaccines, printed as a QR; J2 a community health worker in Country B, offline, reads the foreign QR to register the child and refer, before any verification; J3 the clinic verifies the DVC against the GDHCN trust list and imports it; J4.0 a national portal issues one passcode-protected VHL QR per family member (IPS, DVCs) on one shared phone; J4.1 a clinic abroad scans a VHL, fetches and reads the records. OHS Player and OHS Stack are consumers of the Kotlin library, not part of it: "need to make sure we can do user journey".""" .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/dir-vhl>
    a stt:Document ;
    dcterms:identifier "dir-vhl" ;
    dcterms:title "Stakeholder directive: Verifiable Health Links follow IHE VHL, CBOR map at key 5" ;
    rdfs:comment """Given by the requester on 2026-10-20: subclaim 5 is a Verifiable Health Link; the link payload follows the SMART Health Links payload format in WHO and IHE alike; manifest retrieval, trust and encryption follow the IHE ITI VHL profile (ITI-YY5); the single-file U flow is out of scope; "CBOR map primary", reading a vhlink:/ string too.""" .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/dir-open-standards>
    a stt:Document ;
    dcterms:identifier "dir-open-standards" ;
    dcterms:title "Stakeholder directive: open standards for types and schemas" ;
    rdfs:comment "Given by the requester on 2026-10-20: data types must trace to standardized type systems, with no paywalled ISO standards. Wire format in CDDL; payload models as JSON-LD derived from the FHIR logical models; library API in WIT." .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-intro>
    a stt:Section ;
    dcterms:identifier "qr-intro" ;
    stt:heading "Generating a QR Code" ;
    stt:anchor "generating-a-qr-code" ;
    dcterms:isPartOf <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/doc-qr> ;
    stt:pinnedUrl <https://github.com/WorldHealthOrganization/smart-trust/blob/50bcb25b387d7e7113ffc9e9046452580f9d67aa/input/pagecontent/qr_code_generation.md#generating-a-qr-code> ;
