<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-01>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-01" ;
    dcterms:title "Reference script output is not reproducible byte for byte" ;
    dcterms:description """QR Code Generation 12 and 13 say the script "regenerates the example above byte for byte". It does not. The DSC is signed by the SCA, and the COSE_Sign1 by the DSC, using randomized ECDSA, so every run produces a different DSC, a different kid and different HC1 strings. Running the script at PR head 50bcb25 twice produced kids ZfzK2Csfpsk= and 2sMkNOHFctA=, against WHM+BYqqZiE= in the PR, and different HC1 strings on every run. The committed artefacts are internally consistent: both committed HC1 strings verify against the committed DSC and the kid matches. The sizes in 12.5 are not stable either: the deflated size came out as 283 bytes instead of 282, and the HC1 length as 429 characters instead of 427.""" ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
    stt:resolutionHint """Either use RFC 6979 deterministic ECDSA for both signatures, or reword the claim to "regenerates an equivalent example" and treat the committed JSON and PEM as the normative test vector. The library requirements assume the committed artefacts are the vector (STT-TST-001).""" ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-12> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-13> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/doc-qr-script> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-02>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-02" ;
    dcterms:title "One payload per hcert, or several?" ;
    dcterms:description """QR Code Generation 2 and 4 say an HCERT carries exactly one payload and that -260 is a "map whose single key is the subclaim". HCERT Specification 3.2.7 says "Several different types of health certificate MAY exist under the same claim", and the HCert logical model makes every subclaim 0..1, so it does not rule out more than one. The verifier behaviour for several entries is not specified.""" ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
    stt:resolutionHint "State in hcert_spec 3.2.7 whether more than one subclaim per hcert is allowed and how a verifier treats it." ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-2> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-4> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/hcert-3.2.7> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/doc-sd-hcert> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-03>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-03" ;
    dcterms:title "EKU certificate type for non-DCC payloads is undefined" ;
    dcterms:description """Appendix A.2 defines EKU OIDs for test, vaccinations and recovery, and QR Code Generation 11 step 7 says to check the EKU "against the certificate type". There is no mapping from subclaims 3, 4, 5, -6 or -7 to a certificate type. DVC (-6) is presumably "vaccinations". VHL (5) has no obvious type.""" ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
    stt:resolutionHint "Add a subclaim-to-certificate-type table, or use the GDHCN Key Usage value set." ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-11> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/hcert-A.2> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-04>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-04" ;
    dcterms:title "Base45 reference points at an expired Internet-Draft" ;
    dcterms:description "Both pages cite draft-faltstrom-base45. That draft was published as RFC 9285, which should be the reference." ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-8> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/hcert-4.2.2> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/std-base45-draft> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/std-rfc9285> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-05>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-05" ;
    dcterms:title "CBOR reference RFC 7049 is obsoleted by RFC 8949" ;
    dcterms:description "Neither page says whether issuers should use deterministic encoding, or which rules. The reference script uses length-first canonical ordering (RFC 7049 section 3.9). For the integer and short text keys used here that gives the same order as RFC 8949 core deterministic encoding, but that is luck, not a rule." ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-5> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/hcert-3.2.7> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/std-rfc7049> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/std-rfc8949> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-06>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-06" ;
    dcterms:title "Subclaim 5 is called VHL in one place and SHL in another" ;
    dcterms:description "QR Code Generation 2.1 and the HCert logical model describe subclaim 5 as the URI of a Verifiable Health Link. HCERT Specification 3.2.7.1.5, which is the authoritative list, describes it as Smart Health Link (SHL) and links the SMART Health Links spec. The two define different URI schemes and payloads." ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
    stt:resolutionHint "Raised as WorldHealthOrganization/smart-trust#130: 3.2.7.1.5 becomes Verifiable Health Link (IHE ITI VHL, SHL payload format), and the HCert model types key 5 as the trust-phw VerifiableHealthLinkPayload, carried as a CBOR map. The library follows that (STT-VHL-002)." ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/qr-2.1> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/hcert-3.2.7.1.5> ;
    stt:concerns <https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/doc-sd-hcert> .

<https://github.com/litlfred/smart-trust-tools/kg/id/OI-07>
    a stt:OpenIssue ;
    dcterms:identifier "OI-07" ;
    dcterms:title "iss is a string in the spec but a Coding in the logical model" ;
    dcterms:description "The CWTPayload logical model types claim 1 as Coding. HCERT 3.2.4 and RFC 8392 type it as a string." ;
    stt:upstreamFix true ;
